### QubicaCinema — an administrator changes the programme.
###
### Run the requests top to bottom (VS Code "REST Client", or the HTTP client built into Rider).
###
### Aspire assigns the gateway's port on every run: read the `gateway` endpoint in the dashboard and put it here.
@gateway = http://localhost:5100

# The seeded administrator (local development values, set in src/AppHost/appsettings.json).
@adminEmail = admin@qubicacinema.local
@adminPassword = Admin!Cinema1


### 1. Log in as the administrator.
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}


### 2. Add a film. 201 with a Location and no body.
# @name createMovie
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Long Take",
  "description": "A single shot, ninety minutes, one room.",
  "durationMinutes": 90,
  "genre": "Drama",
  "ageRating": "Teen"
}


### 3. Read it back through the Location the previous response gave. Note the ETag: an edit needs it.
# @name movie
GET {{gateway}}{{createMovie.response.headers.Location}}


### 4. Correct the film. If-Match must carry the ETag of the version being replaced; without it this is a 428,
### and with a stale one it is a 412.
PUT {{gateway}}{{createMovie.response.headers.Location}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{movie.response.headers.ETag}}

{
  "title": "The Long Take",
  "description": "A single shot, ninety minutes, one room. Restored print.",
  "durationMinutes": 90,
  "genre": "Drama",
  "ageRating": "Teen"
}


### 5. Pick a room: the first auditorium in the list.
# @name auditoriums
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/auditoriums


### 6. Schedule the film. 409 if the room is not free for the whole running time; on a second run, change
### startsAt to another evening.
# @name schedule
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/screenings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movieId": "{{movie.response.body.$.id}}",
  "auditoriumId": "{{auditoriums.response.body.$.items[0].id}}",
  "startsAt": "2031-03-14T20:00:00Z",
  "priceAmount": 9.50,
  "priceCurrency": "EUR"
}


### 7. Read the screening. Its seat map appears in Booking within a second or so, through the event bus.
# @name screening
GET {{gateway}}{{schedule.response.headers.Location}}


### 8. Move it an hour later. Same If-Match rule as the film.
PUT {{gateway}}{{schedule.response.headers.Location}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{screening.response.headers.ETag}}

{
  "startsAt": "2031-03-14T21:00:00Z",
  "priceAmount": 9.50,
  "priceCurrency": "EUR"
}


### 9. Call the screening off. A screening is cancelled, never deleted, and every seat booked for it is released.
POST {{gateway}}{{schedule.response.headers.Location}}/cancellation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "projector failure" }
